{"assets":["/editorial-assets/2a83df6821bdf7179e5d97fcacb0bfdfe291c5a4c3bfdffe14815efd6e7c759e.png","/editorial-assets/e340d68f13c375366b0fb0a2cc01562be06c6b4b5611129dedcbfaedcf815533.png"],"contestId":"946","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"problemCode":"946A"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/946/problem/A"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"946A - Partition"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The answer for this problem can be calculated by the next simple formula: "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/2a83df6821bdf7179e5d97fcacb0bfdfe291c5a4c3bfdffe14815efd6e7c759e.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", where |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"| is the absolute value of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"946B"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/946/problem/B"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"946B - Weird Subtraction Process"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The answer can be calculated very easy by Euclid algorithm (which is described in the problem statement), but all subtractions will be replaced by taking by modulo."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"946C"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/946/problem/C"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"946C - String Transformation"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The problem can be solved by the next greedy algorithm. At first we need to store the last character of the alphabet we haven't obtained, for example, in variable "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" (initially it will be equal to 'a'). Then we will just iterate over all characters of the string from left to right and if the current character of the string is not greater than "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", we just replace it to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and increase "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" by 1. If in any moment "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" will be greater than 'z', we got the answer. And if after iterating over the string "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" will be not greater than 'z', the answer is «-1»."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"946D"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/946/problem/D"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"946D - Timetable"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The problem can be solved in the following dynamic programming manner. Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] be the smallest number of hours Ivan can spend in university in the first "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" days while having "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" lessons skipped. To calculate it we can store "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"mn"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] — minimal number of hours Ivan is required to spend in the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th day so that he attends "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" lessons."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then we can iterate over all lengths from 0 to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and update "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"length"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cur"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"] with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"mn"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"length"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cur"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"]."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Precalc works in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nm"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") and dp can be processed in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"nk"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"946E"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/946/problem/E"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"946E - Largest Beautiful Number"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This is pretty typical problem on greedy construction: you are asked to build lexicographically maximal string. In the majority of cases it's done like this. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Imagine you've built some prefix of length "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" with all numbers equal to the prefix of length "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the original string. You are also sure there exists some suffix for it that will give proper beautiful number."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now you have two options: you either put "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" if possible and proceed to the same task of longer prefix or you put the smaller number and fill the entire suffix with the maximum possible beautiful number you can obtain."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now you should learn how to check if any valid suffix exists. It means at least the smallest possible beautiful number with current prefix is smaller than "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It's built like this. Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cnt"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" be the number of digits which currently have odd number of occurences. You put all zeroes but the last "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cnt"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" digits and then output these odd occurence number digits in increasing order. The first part can be checked with partial sums on the number of zeroes on segment in the original string and the second part has its length not greater than 10 and can be checked naively. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Overall complexity: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"|)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"946F"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/946/problem/F"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"946F - Fibonacci String Subsequences"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") was not really large, then we could run the following dynamic programming solution:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] be the number of ways to process first "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" characters of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") so that the suffix of the subsequence of length "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" matches the prefix of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" with length "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". This is not really different from a usual approach with dynamic programming on KMP (constraints in this problem allow us to build KMP automaton naively without the help of any fast prefix-function algorithm). However, the length of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") is really large."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's consider the traversions we make in dynamic programming. Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" be the KMP automaton matrix (that is, let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] be the new value of prefix-function if the previous value was "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and we added a character "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"c"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Then from the state "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"], if the following character is 0, we make traversions to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] and to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"][0]]. This actually leads to rewriting traversions as a matrix. Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" be the vector such that its "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th element is equal to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]. Then advancing from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th character is 0, can be represented as follows: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" × "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"M"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"M"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" can be filled with the help of KMP automaton: for every "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/e340d68f13c375366b0fb0a2cc01562be06c6b4b5611129dedcbfaedcf815533.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" we add 1 to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"M"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"], and also add 1 to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"M"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"][0]]. The same approach can be used to form matrix "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"M"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" that denotes adding character 1, and if we want to add the string "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"), we can actually represent its matrix as "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"M"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"M"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" × "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"M"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This matrix multiplication approach will run in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"xn"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"), but the problem is that it doesn't give us the answer. To obtain it, we may add an auxiliary state "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1 to the dynamic programming, add 1 to it each time we traverse to state "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", multiply it by 2 each time we add a character, and rewrite it into matrix form."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Model solution: "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://pastebin.com/ctSVxmnD"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"https://pastebin.com/ctSVxmnD"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"946G"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/946/problem/G"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"946G - Almost Increasing Array"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If the problem was to make the array strictly increasing, then we could use the following approach: for every element subtract its index from it, find the longest non-decreasing subsequence, and change every element not belonging to this sequence. In this problem we can use a similar technique."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's iterate on the element we will remove after changing everything we need (let's call it "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). For every "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" < "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" we will subtract "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", and for every "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" > "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" we will subtract "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1 from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":". Let's maintain the longest non-decreasing subsequence ending in every element on prefix, and the longest non-decreasing subsequence starting in every element on suffix (this can be done by a lot of different techniques, for example, two segment trees and rollbacking, which is used in our model solution). Then we need to somehow merge these sequences. The easiest way to do it is to consider only the subsequence ending in element "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1 (since if we will need to consider the subsequence ending in some index less than "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1, we would check this possibility choosing other value of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") and use some data structure (BIT, segment tree or something similar) to find the longest subsequence that can be appended to the one we fixed. After checking if we need to delete element "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", we add it to the data structure on prefix, remove element "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1 from the data structure on suffix, check if we have to remove element "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1 and so on."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Model solution: "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://pastebin.com/BiaFgYx6"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"https://pastebin.com/BiaFgYx6"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"}],"kind":"document"},"schema":2,"sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/58210"}